# ---- machine-local paths ----
# Nothing in this repo hardcodes a path on anyone's machine. Each developer copies
# paths.local.ps1.example to paths.local.ps1 and fills in their own. That file is the
# ONLY place a local path is allowed to exist, and it is never committed.
paths.local.ps1
*.local.ps1
!*.local.ps1.example

# ---- build output ----
*.dll
*.exe
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.log
# /analyze output - build.ps1 runs a static-analysis pass, see the note in it
*.nativecodeanalysis.xml

# keep the OpenXR loader out - it is vendored at build time from the SDK
openxr_loader*.dll

# ---- run artefacts ----
last_run.log
run*.log

# ---- NEVER COMMIT ----
# Game-derived data. Ghidra projects contain a full analysis of the game binary, and
# save files are the user's own game data. Both live outside this tree by design; these
# entries exist so an accidental copy cannot slip in.
*.gpr
*.rep/
ghidra_projects/
save_backups/
*.ue3profile*

# extracted or decompiled game content of any kind
uscript/
script_dump/
*.upk
*.u
*.xxx

# ---- tooling local state ----
# Claude Code's per-project settings record absolute paths from this machine. Something
# already excludes this by default, but "already excluded by something" is not a guarantee
# worth trusting with a file that provably contains a user profile path.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---- editor / OS ----
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
